{
  "mn108:0.1": "Middle Discourses 108 ",
  "mn108:0.2": "With Moggallāna the Guardian ",
  "mn108:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn108:1.2": "At one time Venerable Ānanda was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. It was not long after the Buddha had become fully quenched. ",
  "mn108:2.1": "Now at that time King Ajātasattu of Magadha, son of the princess of Videha, being suspicious of King Pajjota, was having Rājagaha fortified. ",
  "mn108:3.1": "Then Venerable Ānanda robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Rājagaha for alms. ",
  "mn108:3.2": "Then it occurred to him, ",
  "mn108:3.3": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Rājagaha. ",
  "mn108:3.4": "Why don’t I go to see the brahmin Moggallāna the Guardian at his place of work?” ",
  "mn108:4.1": "So that’s what he did. ",
  "mn108:4.2": "Moggallāna the Guardian saw Ānanda coming off in the distance ",
  "mn108:4.3": "and said to him, ",
  "mn108:4.4": "“Come, worthy Ānanda! ",
  "mn108:4.5": "Welcome, worthy Ānanda! ",
  "mn108:4.6": "It’s been a long time since you took the opportunity to come here. ",
  "mn108:4.7": "Please, sir, sit down, here, a seat is ready.” ",
  "mn108:4.8": "Ānanda sat down on the seat spread out, ",
  "mn108:4.9": "while Moggallāna took a low seat and sat to one side. ",
  "mn108:4.10": "Then he said to Ānanda, ",
  "mn108:5.1": "“Worthy Ānanda, is there even a single mendicant who has all the same qualities in each and every way as 